    "min": 71,
    "max": 94,
    "mean": 77.3
   },
   "cloud_note": "Every post-event scene is 71-81% cloud. Monsoon-season optical change detection over this corridor is severely limited, which is a direct explanation for why the source geometry remained contested days after the event.",
   "pre_event_gap_months": 35,
   "scenes_covering_detachment_source": 0,
   "source_coverage_note": "No scene in the collection, at any date, contains the detachment source at 85.515 E, 28.271 N. The only scene reaching far enough east is the pre-event acquisition of 17 September 2023, whose footprint stops at 28.261 N, about 1 km south of the source. The detachment area is therefore unimaged by this collection in both epochs, which is a stronger constraint than cloud cover alone and is the reason no detachment volume is estimated.",
   "most_recent_pre_event_covering_syabrubesi": "2023-09-17T05:09:38.085154Z",
   "pre_event_gap_note": "Measured to the most recent pre-event scene whose footprint actually contains Syabrubesi. Two later pre-event scenes exist, of 29 May 2024 and 5 February 2026, but neither covers Syabrubesi or the source, so neither supports change detection at the impacted sites.",
   "_cloud_note": "Range widened on 31 August by a tenth scene at 94 per cent cloud, the worst yet. It covers Syabrubesi but not the source."
  },
